{
  "_readme": [
    "Ratchet for design-system/check-raw-hex.mjs. A file may LOSE colour literals,",
    "never gain one. Regenerate with: node design-system/check-raw-hex.mjs --reseal",
    "",
    "grandfathered — literals that predate the guard. Not endorsed, just not a",
    "regression. Each one is a page that should eventually consume a token.",
    "",
    "openViolations — literals deliberately NOT forgiven. These fail the build.",
    "Nothing lands here by accident; each carries a note saying why."
  ],
  "openViolations": {
    "index.html": {
      "values": {
        "#C4A359": "invented gold shipped by a Cursor agent as --hp-gold; not a palette colour and not derivable from one. The denylist guard could not see it because it only matches the eight retired v1 hex values. This is the regression this guard exists for — it is not grandfathered on purpose. Fix: use var(--tangerine) (ΔG, 8.86:1) or, if a genuinely new hue is wanted, add it to tokens.css with a measured contrast ratio first.",
        "#8A6E2F": "the light-mode partner of --hp-gold, same origin, same fix."
      }
    }
  },
